Wire the vendored MinUI module into the frontend, and make the artifacts the
launcher reads match what it expects.

The module itself lives in overlay/ in the pak repo and is copied into the tree
by the Makefile before this patch is applied, so nothing here adds a file. That
keeps the patch to modifications of existing ones and small enough to rebase on
an upstream tag, which matters because DSperate ships tags weekly.

What it changes:

  CMakeLists.txt      builds minui.cpp and the pause menu (minui_menu.cpp,
                      minui_gfx.cpp, and the stb implementations in
                      minui_stb.cpp, built with -w) into dsperate, via
                      target_sources rather than the add_executable list so a
                      change to either never conflicts with the other.
  main.cpp            polls the power button once a frame (short press sleeps,
                      a held press quits through the ordinary exit path so the
                      battery save and auto state are written); writes the
                      launcher's slot thumbnail and marker whenever the player
                      saves or loads a user slot, and drops them when the
                      pause menu deletes it; adds the emu.state_key option;
                      renames screenshots; declares the pause menu as
                      MinUiMenu instead of Menu, and spoils the MENU tap when
                      the launcher's MENU+VOL chord was pressed; has the
                      pause menu name the layout, main screen or PiP corner
                      a hotkey just picked, in a notice that fades out; and
                      stops the audio before the game switcher's save, which
                      otherwise runs the device dry.
  input.{h,cpp}       a game_switcher hotkey action, unbound by default because
                      mod+back is already layout_next upstream. A launcher that
                      wants it binds it in its own config. spoil_mod_tap(), so
                      a modifier press SDL never saw used is not a tap.
  config.cpp          documents emu.state_key.
  tests/CMakeLists    registers test_minui_menu, the pause menu's suite.

menu.h and menu.cpp are deliberately untouched. MinUiMenu has Menu's public
API and uses Menu's own public types, and reaches settings, bindings, cheats
and achievements only through SettingsHost, CheevosHost and the Setting
tables, so a refactor of upstream's menu internals cannot break it silently.

Thumbnails go through the existing write_png() at the .bmp path the launcher
looks for, which is exactly what NextUI itself writes there: both frontends
load them with IMG_Load, which dispatches on the magic bytes rather than the
extension. write_png is otherwise untouched.

emu.state_key defaults to "code", so an upstream build behaves exactly as it
did. "rom" keys states on the ROM filename instead, which is what a launcher
keys its own files on, and stops two hacks of one game sharing slots.

The screenshot rename is not configurable: <GAMECODE>-<timestamp>.png became
<display name>.<YYYY-MM-DD-HH-MM-SS>.png, which is what NextUI's minarch writes
and so what every other system on the card writes, with the display name
worked out as NextUI works it out, map.txt alias included. A screenshot also
puts up "Screenshot saved" unless NextUI's notifyScreenshot is off.
